From 7f58cd9e9fd98319c242375040bb1aae6057d726 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: duncanmcqueen <206344294+duncanmcqueen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 08:27:27 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Add the Haiku AWT and sound peer, and fixes for Kaffe on
 Haiku

- gnu.java.awt.peer.haiku: an AWT toolkit with native Haiku windows,
  menus, file panels, cursors, clipboard (text, pictures, files, MIME
  data), drag and drop, printing (BPrintJob), input methods, modal and
  always-on-top windows. Text is measured and drawn with Haiku's fonts
  (HaikuFontPeer: BFont metrics, app_server rendering, glyph outlines).
- gnu.javax.sound.sampled.haiku: a javax.sound mixer that plays
  through the Haiku media server.
- native/jni/haiku-peer: libhaikupeer (-lbe -ltracker -lmedia
  -ltranslation); include/Makefile.am makes its JNI headers.
- configure: --enable-haiku-peer, on by default on Haiku. It makes
  HaikuToolkit the default toolkit and registers the Haiku mixer.
  Look for socket functions in libnetwork too. Remove the stray
  spaces after 'statvfs \', which made new autoconf skip mmap.
- lib/Makefile.am: copy the service files that configure makes, so
  out-of-tree builds get them.
- cpnet.c: use gethostbyname_r only when its declaration is known.
- OpenTypeFontPeer: implement canDisplay() and canDisplayUpTo().
- Frame.setState() set the opposite state.
- PrinterJob.getPrinterJob() uses the java.awt.printerjob property.
- DragSource made only one drag context and reused it for every drag.
- DropTargetDragEvent and DropTargetDropEvent rejected all valid source
  actions; DropTargetContext.getCurrentDataFlavors() returned null,
  and its target actions were always 0 (it now asks the peer).
- Thread: create the thread-local map on first use (Kaffe).
- ResolverCache: create the cache before the TTLs.
- VMNetworkInterface: define IFF_RUNNING if missing (Haiku).

Run autoreconf -fi after applying this patch.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
